    <string name="speech_fish_language">Fish Audio language and pronunciation</string>
    <string name="speech_fish_language_hint">Language affects text normalization only, not the speech model, accent or output language. The pronunciation dictionary accepts a JSON array of up to 3 entries.</string>
    <string name="speech_fish_paging_stalled">Voice pagination did not advance. Refresh or narrow your search.</string>
    <string name="speech_fish_references_hint">Import WAV, MP3 or FLAC and enter the words actually spoken. Clear 10–30 second speech is recommended. Up to 8 speaker groups, 4 samples per group and 8 MiB total (module limits). Samples are excluded from configuration backups. In this mode the selected audio and its transcript are sent to Fish with each TTS request.</string>
    <string name="speech_fish_s1_loudness_hint">S1 does not use loudness normalization. Your saved setting is retained.</string>
    <string name="speech_fish_s1_tags">S1 uses fixed parenthesized tags, for example (happy)你好。</string>
    <string name="speech_fish_s2_tags">S2 models accept natural language instructions in square brackets, for example [softly]你好。</string>
    <string name="speech_fish_scope_title">Single speaker voices · %1$s\n%2$s</string>
    <string name="speech_fish_speakers_hint">Configure voices in speaker:0, speaker:1 order as used in the text, up to 8 speakers (module editing limit). One voice may serve multiple speakers. S1 does not support this mode.</string>
    <string name="speech_fish_tags_guide">%1$s\n\nMultiple speakers use numbered tags, for example &lt;|speaker:0|&gt;你好。&lt;|speaker:1|&gt;你好呀。 IDs match the voice list or reference audio groups, starting at 0.\n\nWrite these tags in the original text yourself. The module does not insert them into automatic replies or comments.</string>
    <string name="speech_fish_title_language_hint">Filter Fish voice titles by language ID, one per line. Saved separately from voice language; leave empty for any language.</string>
    <string name="speech_fish_voice">Fish Audio voice settings</string>
    <string name="speech_fish_voice_language_hint">Enter Fish catalog language IDs, one per line, such as zh or en. Multiple entries are allowed. Saving replaces the current voice language list; leave empty for any language.</string>
